no-fw-svn-limited: no firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchies

Classification: profile setting.

tpm-rs does not implement firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchies (TPM 2.0
Part 1, "Firmware-limited Hierarchy": "a hierarchy whose seed and proof values
are derived from a Primary Seed and a Firmware Secret"; "SVN-limited
Hierarchy": "a hierarchy whose seed and proof values are derived from a
Primary Seed and a Firmware SVN Secret"). These are the TPM_RH_FW_* and
SVN-limited handle rows of TPM 2.0 Part 2, Table "Definition of (TPM_HANDLE)
TPMI_RH_HIERARCHY Type": "TPM_RH_FW_OWNER | Firmware-limited Storage
hierarchy", "TPM_RH_FW_PLATFORM", "TPM_RH_FW_ENDORSEMENT", "TPM_RH_FW_NULL",
"{SVN_OWNER_FIRST:SVN_OWNER_LAST} | SVN-limited Storage hierarchies",
"{SVN_PLATFORM_FIRST:SVN_PLATFORM_LAST}",
"{SVN_ENDORSEMENT_FIRST:SVN_ENDORSEMENT_LAST}" and
"{SVN_NULL_FIRST:SVN_NULL_LAST}". The reference profile enables both
(FW_LIMITED_SUPPORT and SVN_LIMITED_SUPPORT = YES); they are disabled so that
the reference implements the same hierarchies as tpm-rs: the handles are not
listed by TPM2_GetCapability (TPM_CAP_HANDLES, TPM_CAP_AUTH_POLICIES). They
remain TPMI_RH_HIERARCHY values (the unmarshaling code is unconditional);
commands that use them fail with TPM_RC_FW_LIMITED/TPM_RC_SVN_LIMITED where
the reference needs the (unavailable) firmware secret.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
--- a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
@@ -232,8 +232,8 @@
 //***********************************************
 // Defines controlling Firmware- and SVN-limited objects
 //***********************************************
-#define FW_LIMITED_SUPPORT                    YES
-#define SVN_LIMITED_SUPPORT                   YES
+#define FW_LIMITED_SUPPORT                    NO
+#define SVN_LIMITED_SUPPORT                   NO
 
 //***********************************************
 // Defines controlling External NV
